    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0878" n="868" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg868"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Colonel J. Hart
                            Caughey
                    </hi><anchor n="33" xml:id="d570-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to Mr. Tung Pi-wu
                    </hi><anchor n="34" xml:id="d570-f2"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">OSE 306</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-07-19">July 19, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I received the attached memorandum (Inch 1) over the telephone this morning from
                    General Chou En-lai.</p>
                <p>As requested by General Chou, I attach as Inch 2<anchor n="35" xml:id="d570-f3"/>
                    the reference message received by Police Office, Peiping, regarding the seven
                    American enlisted Marines.</p>


                <xi:include href="d570-a1.xml" xpointer="d570-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d570-f1" n="33" type="source" xml:id="d570-f1-content">
                <p>Executive Officer on General Marshall’s staff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d570-f2" n="34" xml:id="d570-f2-content">
                <p>Member of the Chinese Communist Party delegation at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d570-f3" n="35" xml:id="d570-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 170054Z, July 17, not printed; this telegram from Admiral Cooke to
                    General Marshall transmitted original telegram No. 161132Z by Army Radio,
                    Peiping, which reported the kidnapping under reference. Further information on
                    the incident was reported in telegram No. 170549Z, July 19, from General Rockey
                    to Admiral Cooke: “1830 13 July while procuring ice 8 enlisted men of ‘C’
                    Company 7th Marines stationed at bridges 99–102 were ambushed at village 1½
                    miles southeast of Liu Shu Ying which is about 15 miles from Peitaiho junction
                    on Peiping–Mukden railroad by a group of reportedly 80 Communists or bandits.
                    Seven enlisted captured and now in hands of the Communist or dissident band. One
                    enlisted escaped and now in our hands. Strong patrols were dispatched promptly
                    to comb surrounding country.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
